# code-standards vendored .prettierignore. Edit upstream and `code-standards sync`.
#
# Prettier must NOT format two kinds of file:
#   1. generated / build output — it isn't source.
#   2. files code-standards vendors verbatim — reformatting them would drift them
#      from their upstream template and trip `code-standards sync`.
# Everything else (your real source) is yours to format: `prettier --write .`.

# Generated / build output
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/
coverage/

# Python tooling artifacts (a TS repo may still carry these)
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/

# code-standards-vendored files (owned upstream; formatted there, not here)
.github/workflows/quality.yml
.pre-commit-config.yaml
eslint.config.mjs
.prettierrc
tsconfig.base.json

# code-standards-GENERATED files. Same rule, different mechanism: these are not
# copied from a template but rendered/merged by the tool itself (dependabot.yml by
# `vendor_dependabot`, the CLAUDE.md stanza by `inject_stanza`), so prettier
# reformatting them starts a tug-of-war with the next `sync`. Omitting these two
# is why agent-sites and rate-shift-calculator have had a red CI since
# 2026-06-30 on files neither repo wrote.
.github/dependabot.yml
CLAUDE.md

# portfolio-toolkit-managed (owned by project-standards, not code-standards) —
# the backlog skill / `portfolio add` rewrite this; formatting it just starts a
# tug-of-war the next portfolio write undoes.
PROJECT.md
